"Symmetric edge polytopes are not gamma-positive (https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.02424)\nciteturn7academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Title: Symmetric edge polytopes are not gamma-positive ... Date: Thu Jul  2 16:52:48 2026\n\nA conjecture posed by Ohsugi and Tsuchiya (2019) postulates that the Ehrhart $h^*$-polynomials of symmetric edge polytopes are $γ$-positive.\nTitle: Symmetric edge polytopes are not gamma-positive\nAuthors: Luis Ferroni\nDate: Thu Jul  2 16:52:48 2026\n\nA conjecture posed by Ohsugi and Tsuchiya (2019) postulates that the Ehrhart $h^*$-polynomials of symmetric edge polytopes are $γ$-positive. We disprove this conjecture by exhibiting an infinite family of counterexamples. The smallest example provided by our construction is a $36$-dimensional symmetric edge polytope.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe number of edges of a symmetric edge polytope (https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.16572)\nciteturn7academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; Title: The number of edges of a symmetric edge polytope\nTitle: The number of edges of a symmetric edge polytope\nAuthors: Giulia Codenotti, Roberto Riccardi, Lorenzo Venturello\nDate: Thu Dec 18 14:12:49 2025\n\nThe symmetric edge polytope of a simple graph is a lattice polytope defined as the convex hull of a subset of the type A roots corresponding to the edges of the graph. In this article we prove a sharp lower bound for the number of edges of the symmetric edge polytope of a graph as a function of elementary graph invariants. Moreover, we characterize graphs attaining this bound. We highlight a connection with the h*-polynomial of such polytopes and, motivated by a conjecture of Ohsugi and Tsuchiya, we investigate the behaviour of such polynomial under edge-deletion in the graph.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(PDF) The number of edges of a symmetric edge polytope (https://www.researchg